// KEYWORD float

// KEYWORD for
// for (initial; condition; aftereach) { body; }      
// For loop.

// KEYWORD if
// if (test) { body1; } else { body2; }
// If test is true (non-zero), execute body1.  
// Otherwise execute body2 (optional)


<pre>
if (<i>test</i>) { <i>body;</i> }
</pre>

The simplest if statement has two parts: a test and a body.  First,
the test is performed.  Second, *if the test succeeded, body will be
executed.<br><br>

Example:<br>

<pre>
// If analog sensor 4 reads higher than 100, turn motor 0 on forwards
if (analog(4)>100) {
  fd(0);
}
</pre>

The if statement can also have an <b>else</b> clause.  



  if

1. Test the condition


